From 994fa6dfc56de7a984abbbd905918628dd335104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:01:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Intercept device DNS setting for resolvers in front of Forkop

Requires: 024-excluded-devices

New settings option intercept_device_dns (default on, no behaviour
change). When a resolver such as AdGuard Home listens on :53 and
forwards to Forkop (127.0.0.42:53), Forkop still redirected the DNS of
excluded devices (:1605) and of devices named in section device filters
(:1603) before the resolver saw it. The resolver then only saw
127.0.0.1: no per-client statistics, query log, filtering or blocked
services for those devices.

With the option off:

- nft: no DNS redirect for excluded devices, and the source-aware DNS
  set only keeps devices of DNS-action sections (a per-device DNS server
  cannot work without seeing the client);
- excluded devices may now receive FakeIP answers from the resolver.
  Their traffic to the FakeIP ranges is marked and sent with TPROXY to a
  new excluded-tproxy-in inbound (:1606, placed before the generic
  TPROXY rules), which sing-box routes to bypass-out: the connection
  goes direct to the real domain. Other traffic of these devices still
  leaves the mangle chain early, as before;
- sing-box: DNS rules of bypass/connection sections no longer depend on
  the client. Device-filtered section domains resolve to FakeIP for
  everyone and the route rule, which still matches the source address,
  decides per device.

Tests: tests/device_dns_intercept.sh (nft commands and order, DNS source
set, sing-box 1.13/1.14 config, optional sing-box check). Checked live
with AdGuard Home v0.107.79 and sing-box-extended 1.14.1 in network
namespaces: AdGuard Home sees every client and blocks per client,
excluded devices (IP and MAC) and a bypass device reach FakeIP domains
directly, a normal client is still proxied.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HEQfjBzS7Wos7AvTk18TDQ
